== is the access width a function of the carrier? ==
  tight packing rule                 NOT a function: 432 pairs, first W=1 and W=3 share the divisor and need 8 and 16
  loose packing rule                 NOT a function: 651 pairs, first W=1 and W=2 share the divisor and need 8 and 16

== and the carrier, a function of the access width? ==
  tight packing rule                 NOT a function: 416 pairs, first W=3 and W=9 share the divisor and need 8 and 16
  loose packing rule                 NOT a function: 644 pairs, first W=2 and W=9 share the divisor and need 8 and 16

== controls ==
  C1 access := carrier               is a function (0 violating pairs)
  C2 access := const u8, forward     is a function (0 violating pairs)
  C2 access := const u8, reverse     NOT a function: 5440 pairs, first W=1 and W=9 share the divisor and need 8 and 16
  C3 planted single violation        NOT a function: 7 pairs, first W=1 and W=5 share the divisor and need 8 and 64

== verdict ==
  C1 a rule equal to the carrier reports zero:        true
  C2 a constant rule reports zero forward, nonzero reverse: true
  C3 the planted violation is found and nothing else: true
  neither determines the other, under both packing rules: true

  RESULT: carrier and access width are two independent facts of the declared width
